      "body": "## Summary\n\nFix Kimi-K3 AR fusion prefill buffer overflow when attention data parallelism (DP) is enabled.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`_max_buffer_rows()` in `k3_ar_fusion.py` computed the buffer capacity from the per-chunk prefill size (or `max_prefill_tokens`) without accounting for attention data parallelism. When attention-DP is enabled, multiple DP ranks can be batched together, so the runtime token count can exceed the per-chunk limit. This caused the pre-allocated buffer to be too small, leading to out-of-bounds writes or incorrect AR fusion results during prefill.\n\n## Fix\n\nScale the base buffer rows by `attn_dp_size` when it is greater than 1. The buffer capacity is now `base_rows * attn_dp_size`, ensuring sufficient space for the combined token count across all DP ranks.\n\n**File changed:** `python/sglang/srt/layers/communication/k3_ar_fusion.py`\n\n## Testing\n\n- Verified Kimi-K3 AR fusion prefill works correctly with attention-DP enabled (multi-rank batching).\n- When `attn_dp_size == 1` (default), the behavior is unchanged.\n\nCloses #46447\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40259175048](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40259175048)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40259174891](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40259174891)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40259175003](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40259175003)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
